				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "We want to use an LLM to create the model from the dataset rather than creating it by hand. We have several examples in the book. One is the GitHub REST API example. Another is the Molding CSV data tutorial: {{gtPage:Tutorial: molding CSV data into an explainable system|db=2j9m7db2i4oz116bexd7wbdxo}}, which is based on exactly this dataset. Note that the tutorial only works with the first file listing all the papers, and does not touch the actual design study papers, so we can use the tutorial to guide the creation of a new model."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-08-26T09:19:49.178819+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-08-26T09:20:52.495157+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "tFRV8K51S72A8WnOgU8i8w=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Note that to avoid parsing issues, the tutorial uses versions of the CSV files that have beem converted to UTF-8. See {{gtMethod:name=VRTutorialExamples>>#datasetFolder}}. We copy those to our local data folder."
			},
